      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture of the original test. I'll improve understandability by:\n1. Removing all unused imports and fields\n2. Breaking the single flat test into focused, well-named test methods grouped with `@Nested` classes\n3. Adding brief comments only where behavior is non-obvious (e.g., out-of-bounds offset)The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports and the unused `WINDOWS` field, and reorganizes the 24 flat assertions into 3 `@Nested` classes (`WhenOffsetIsZero`, `WhenOffsetIsOne`, `WhenInputsAreNull`) with individually named `@Test` methods — making the intent of each assertion immediately clear from the method name alone."
